Google's "G" is docs/specs/assets/google-g.svg, which logos.rs takes from the
spec as it is, for People and for Sign in. It is Google's "G" as Google's own
"Sign in with Google" button draws it, from the credential_button_library
script that https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client loads, with only the SVG's
class left out. It is drawn unchanged, as Google's branding guidelines
(https://developers.google.com/identity/branding-guidelines) allow, to stand
for signing in with Google. Google and the Google logo are trademarks of
Google LLC.
